  "tldr": "A single response-adaptive experiment must allocate observations for an entire quantile treatment-effect curve while preserving optional-stopping validity. The proposal defines integrated whole-curve Neyman regret and worst-quantile LIL width from the same finite-population score-energy kernel, proves that their sharp achievable pairs are the lower Pareto envelope of a one-dimensional allocation map with a KKT certificate, constructs an observable realized-variance QTE band attaining the width coordinate, and isolates oracle-free logarithmic-regret attainment as the central open problem.",
