    "gap": "Published QTE design theory optimizes a fixed quantile at a fixed horizon, while published anytime Neyman-regret theory and adaptive confidence sequences concern scalar means. Time-uniform CDF work does not characterize the design that balances average whole-curve efficiency against the worst local quantile width.",
